From eb043a6685f9137eef300fb7e4c452a2f3c7c504 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:50:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Flow mode: the survey's behaviour as a canvas (Phase 3)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The fourth environment. The engine's `buildLogicFlow` was already the graph
— pages or questions as nodes, every way a respondent moves between them as
an edge, branches and loops and skips and quota exits included — and the
Logic panel printed it as text. Now it is drawn, laid out, and answers the
two questions the brief asks of it.

  · Edges are TYPED at the source. `LogicFlowEdge.kind` (sequence · gate ·
    branch · otherwise · skip · loop · quota) is an optional schema field
    set by `buildLogicFlow`, so a canvas colours by meaning rather than by
    guessing from labels; old graphs classify by label as a fallback.

  · Layout is hand-rolled (lib/flow/layout.ts, 8 tests): cycles broken
    (loop returns and backward skips become side-routed back edges),
    longest-path layering, barycentre ordering, a stored position pins a
    node. 600 questions lay out in 4 ms; the canvas opens on pages for
    surveys over 150 questions and on questions below (switchable).

  · Select a node and the canvas shows WHAT CAN REACH IT (upstream, cyan)
    and WHAT IT CAN AFFECT (downstream via the routing graph plus whatever
    the dependency index says reads it, amber); the edges between them
    light; everything else recedes — harder in Focus. The inspector from
    Architect sits beside it, so a branch's DEPENDS ON is one click from
    its arms.

  · Debug mode (lib/flow/debug.ts, 5 tests): type "Q2=A, Q1=30, Q11=1|3"
    and a headless respondent WALKS the survey with those answers through
    the real engine — so skips fire and loops repeat, not a compile — and
    the taken path lights. The suite proves the same walk routes through
    the Business arm or the Consumer arm on one answer, and screens out on
    "no consent".

  · Editing goes through the Survey Flow panel's own functions: dragging a
    node stores its position on def.logicFlow by id (Auto-arrange forgets
    them); dropping a node onto a container calls canDropFlowNode and
    moveFlowNode, refusing with the engine's reason; "+ Add…" inserts
    through the command registry and selects the new element. Pan, wheel
    and ⌘-wheel zoom, fit, a minimap, search that centres on its match,
    double-click to open in Architect.

Tests: scripts/flow-mode-test.mjs (38, clean console, 600-question budget:
463 ms to render, 10 zoom steps in 292 ms). Mutation-checked: highlight
direction flipped, drop that never moves, debug that ignores answers —
each caught. Sweep green: multimodal-foundation, grid-mode (45),
architect-mode (32), context-right-panel, canvas (38), flow-dnd,
flow-export, logic-builder, save-integrity. Studio lib: 148. Engine
logicGraph tests unchanged: 19.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
